```react
function App() {
  const [title, setTitle] = React.useState("Draft");
  return <main><label htmlFor="title">Notebook title</label>
    <input id="title" value={title} onChange={event => setTitle(event.target.value)} />
    <p role="status">Title: {title}</p>
    <button onClick={() => setTitle("")}>Clear</button>
  </main>;
}
```
This version starts with Draft. Erasing all text is a valid change to an empty string, not missing state.

after:
```react
function App() {
  const [title, setTitle] = React.useState("");
  return (
    <main>
      <label htmlFor="title">Notebook title</label>
      <input
        id="title"
        value={title}
        onChange={event => setTitle(event.target.value)}
      />
      <p role="status">Title: {title}</p>
      <button onClick={() => setTitle("")}>Clear</button>
    </main>
  );
}
```
Typing `Orbit` makes both the field and message use that text. Clear changes the state to empty text, so both update.
